HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor
HiddenServiceVersion 3
HiddenServicePort 5222 directory_server:5222

# Onion service DoS defenses. These are per-service options and must stay
# below the HiddenServiceDir line above.
#
# Introduction rate limiting (Tor 0.4.2+): introduction points drop INTRODUCE2
# cells above this rate, so a flood of connection attempts is absorbed by the
# relays instead of this host. Normal directory traffic is far below the
# limit, so honest clients are unaffected.
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSDefense 1
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSRatePerSec 25
HiddenServiceEnableIntroDoSBurstPerSec 200
# Streams per rendezvous circuit: honest peers open one connection per
# circuit, while a sybil flood can multiplex thousands of connections over a
# few circuits and so bypass introduction limits and PoW. Exceeding the limit
# closes the whole circuit, forcing the client to pay for a new introduction.
HiddenServiceMaxStreams 10
HiddenServiceMaxStreamsCloseCircuit 1

# Proof of work (Tor 0.4.8+): clients must solve a puzzle whose effort scales
# with the rendezvous backlog, so a flood costs the attacker CPU. The effort
# starts at zero and only rises under load. It requires a Tor built with the
# pow module (`tor --list-modules` must show `pow: yes`, which needs
# `--enable-gpl` at build time); Tor refuses to start when these options are
# set on a build without it. Uncomment once your Tor image has the module.
#HiddenServicePoWDefensesEnabled 1
#HiddenServicePoWQueueRate 25
#HiddenServicePoWQueueBurst 250
